FN-XD131ZE
FISCAL NOTE
House Bill 487
Committee: Ways and Means General Fund Sponsor: Representative Rex Reynolds
Analyst: Tiffany Weaver Date: 02/23/2026
House Bill 487 as introduced would appropriate a total of $43,138,650 from the Opioid
Treatment and Abatement Fund for fiscal year 2026 to the following entities in the following
amounts:
 Board of Pardons and Paroles: $1.5 million;
 Department of Mental Health: $26,360,000;
 Auburn University: $1.9 million;
 University of Alabama at Birmingham: $2 million;
 USA Health University of South Alabama: $1.1 million;
 Administrative Office of Courts for Specialty Courts: $3 million;
 District Attorneys: $2.1 million;
 Child Advocacy Centers: $2,136,650
 Office of Prosecution Services: $1,092,000;
 Department of Forensic Sciences: $450,000;
 Department of Senior Services: $500,000;
 Department of Corrections: $1 million.
This bill would also provide that these funds would not revert at the end of fiscal year 2026 but
would carry forward for the purposes appropriated.
